    <item>
      <title>Overview</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/overview/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/overview/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LeMat-Synth&lt;/strong&gt; is an open-source multi-modal toolbox for extracting structured synthesis procedures and performance data from materials science literature at scale. It was presented at &lt;a href=&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.26824&#34;&gt;NeurIPS AI4Mat 2025&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Installation</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/installation/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/installation/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;prerequisites&#34;&gt;Prerequisites&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python 3.11+&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/astral-sh/uv&#34;&gt;uv&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; — the package manager used by this project&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Install &lt;code&gt;uv&lt;/code&gt; (one-time):&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expressive-code&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure class=&#34;frame is-terminal not-content&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figcaption class=&#34;header&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;title&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh &lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; sh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;install-the-package&#34;&gt;Install the package&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expressive-code&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure class=&#34;frame is-terminal not-content&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figcaption class=&#34;header&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;title&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# 1. Clone the repository&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;git clone https://github.com/LeMaterial/lematerial-llm-synthesis.git&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; lematerial-llm-synthesis&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# 2. Create a virtual environment and install all dependencies&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;uv sync&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# 3. Install the llm_synthesis package in editable mode&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;uv pip install -e .&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# 4. Verify the installation&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;uv run python -c &lt;span class=&#34;s2&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;import llm_synthesis; print(&amp;#39;OK&amp;#39;)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;set-up-api-keys&#34;&gt;Set up API keys&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Copy the example environment file and add your keys:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Quickstart</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/quickstart/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/quickstart/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This page gets you from zero to your first extracted synthesis in under 10 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;option-1--interactive-notebook-recommended-for-beginners&#34;&gt;Option 1 — Interactive notebook (recommended for beginners)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Open the tutorial notebooks in Jupyter:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Dataset Access</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/dataset/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/getting-started/dataset/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;LeMat-Synth publishes two datasets on the HuggingFace Hub. Both are &lt;strong&gt;gated&lt;/strong&gt; —&#xA;access is granted automatically, but you must request it once and be&#xA;authenticated.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Tutorials</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/tutorials/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/tutorials/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Seven runnable notebooks that take you from &lt;em&gt;reading&lt;/em&gt; LeMat-Synth data to&#xA;&lt;em&gt;producing&lt;/em&gt; it, and finally to &lt;em&gt;changing what gets produced&lt;/em&gt;. Each one is&#xA;self-contained, states its prerequisites and cost up front, and explains what&#xA;every step is doing rather than just executing it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Thermocatalysis</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/thermocatalysis/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/thermocatalysis/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;End-to-end workflow for ammonia-decomposition catalysts: extract synthesis&#xA;procedures &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; conversion-vs-temperature curves from a folder of PDFs, then&#xA;score several vision models against human-annotated ground truth.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Superconductors</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/superconductors/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/superconductors/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Extracts synthesis procedures and critical temperatures (&lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt;&lt;sub&gt;c&lt;/sub&gt;) from&#xA;superconductor papers. &lt;em&gt;T&lt;/em&gt;&lt;sub&gt;c&lt;/sub&gt; is read twice — once from the text, and&#xA;once geometrically from ρ(T) or R(T) plots — which gives a built-in&#xA;cross-check on both readings.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Porous Materials</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/porosity/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/porosity/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Extracts synthesis procedures and adsorption isotherms from papers on MOFs,&#xA;zeolites, COFs and related frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is the simplest of the three case studies — no domain metric extractors, no&#xA;custom writer — which makes it the best template to copy when starting a new&#xA;domain. &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/custom-domain/&#34;&gt;Building your own case study&lt;/a&gt; walks through exactly&#xA;how it is assembled.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Build Your Own</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/custom-domain/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/case-studies/custom-domain/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Pointing LeMat-Synth at a new scientific domain — electrochemistry, battery&#xA;cycling, thermoelectrics, photocatalysis — does not require touching the&#xA;pipeline. You assemble a &lt;code&gt;DomainConfig&lt;/code&gt; from four pieces and hand it to&#xA;&lt;code&gt;BatchRunner&lt;/code&gt;, which already knows how to find PDFs, detect supplementary&#xA;files, retry on rate limits, resume interrupted runs, and report progress.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CLI Reference</title>
      <link>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/user-guide/cli/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:61375/lemat-synth/user-guide/cli/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;lemat-synth&lt;/code&gt; command-line tool lets you extract structured synthesis&#xA;procedures from materials science papers without writing any Python code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expressive-code&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figure class=&#34;frame is-terminal not-content&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;figcaption class=&#34;header&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;title&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;lemat-synth extract &amp;lt;paper&amp;gt;   &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nv&#34;&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;value ...&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Extract from a single paper&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;lemat-synth batch   &amp;lt;folder&amp;gt;  &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nv&#34;&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;value ...&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# Extract from a folder of papers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Both commands accept the same &lt;code&gt;key=value&lt;/code&gt; overrides, which can be used to change models, prompts, output paths, and other settings. See &lt;a href=&#34;#quick-reference-all-arguments&#34;&gt;Quick Reference: All Arguments&lt;/a&gt; below.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
